        81.83369445800781
      ],
      "text": "Recommendation 11  on use of CXR for people with HIV was first made in 2018 to update the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        79.31470489501953,
        527.4059448242188,
        95.03370666503906
      ],
      "text": "(26) position in the 2011 guidelines  . Since 2021, WHO has also conditionally recommended use of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        93.79071807861328,
        527.4345703125,
        108.23371887207031
      ],
      "text": "CAD software programmes to interpret digital CXRs for pulmonary TB during screening and triage",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        105.71472930908203,
        327.2587890625,
        121.43373107910156
      ],
      "text": "(13) of people aged ≥ 15 years, regardless of HIV status  .",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        128.69459533691406,
        527.549560546875,
        143.13758850097656
      ],
      "text": "Use of CXR for screening in parallel with symptom screening improves the sensitivity over that with the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.970510482788086,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        141.8946075439453,
        527.6160278320312,
        156.3376007080078
      ],
      "text": "W4SS alone in all subgroups of people with HIV. In particular, screening with CXR significantly improves",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.963689804077148,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        155.09474182128906,
        527.4453735351562,
        169.53773498535156
      ],
      "text": "the sensitivity in people with HIV who are on ART and is the most sensitive screening strategy for this",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        168.2947540283203,
        527.37744140625,
        182.7377471923828
      ],
      "text": "group. When available, CXR is recommended for use in parallel with the W4SS to rule out TB disease",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        180.2187042236328,
        527.4254760742188,
        195.93775939941406
      ],
      "text": "(13) . The evidence on the performance of  before initiating TPT in people with HIV who are on ART",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        194.69471740722656,
        527.4390258789062,
        209.13771057128906
      ],
      "text": "CXR and the W4SS for all people with HIV reviewed before making the 2021 TB screening guidelines",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        207.8946075439453,
        527.062255859375,
        222.3376007080078
      ],
      "text": "was from eight studies, conducted in Benin, Botswana, Brazil, Guinea, India, Kenya, Malawi, Myanmar,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.988794326782227,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        221.09474182128906,
        376.1571044921875,
        235.53773498535156
      ],
      "text": "Peru, South Africa and Zimbabwe, with a total of 6238 participants (",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        376.177001953125,
        221.09474182128906,
        407.6986083984375,
        235.53773498535156
      ],
      "text": "Table 3",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        407.7001037597656,
        221.09474182128906,
        527.4202270507812,
        235.53773498535156
      ],
      "text": "). CXR alone was found to",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86614990234375,
        234.2947540283203,
        527.4374389648438,
        248.7377471923828
      ],
      "text": "have similar sensitivity to and similar or higher specificity than the W4SS in all subpopulations. When",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86614990234375,
        247.49476623535156,
        527.3764038085938,
        261.9377746582031
      ],
      "text": "CXR was conducted after a positive W4SS, CXR was less or similarly sensitive and more or similarly",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86614990234375,
        260.69476318359375,
        527.3960571289062,
        275.1377868652344
      ],
      "text": "specific. When CXR was used in parallel with the W4SS, the sensitivity was higher or similar and the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86614990234375,
        273.89459228515625,
        168.0431365966797,
        288.3376770019531
      ],
      "text": "similar. specificity was",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        295.4886474609375,
        527.5471801757812,
        310.0416564941406
      ],
      "text": "Recommendation 12  relates to the use of CRP for screening adults and adolescents with HIV for TB",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 10.999099731445312,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        308.798583984375,
        527.4266357421875,
        323.2416076660156
      ],
      "text": "disease. CRP is an indicator of general inflammation that can be measured with point-of-care tests in",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        321.99859619140625,
        527.4351806640625,
        336.4416198730469
      ],
      "text": "capillary blood collected by finger prick. The evidence reviewed comprised six studies conducted in",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        333.922607421875,
        527.4420776367188,
        349.6416320800781
      ],
      "text": "(13) Kenya, South Africa and Uganda with a total of 3971 participants  . The accuracy of CRP based on",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        348.39862060546875,
        527.377197265625,
        362.8416442871094
      ],
      "text": "cut-off values of > 5 mg/L and > 10 mg/L as indicators of TB disease was reviewed, and the accuracy",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        361.5986328125,
        527.4091186523438,
        376.0416564941406
      ],
      "text": "of two was considered to be similar or superior to that of the W4SS. The cut-off value of > 5 mg/L",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        374.79864501953125,
        527.389892578125,
        389.2416687011719
      ],
      "text": "was recommended, as it is the lowest threshold for abnormality in many clinical settings and is more",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        387.9986572265625,
        527.4168701171875,
        402.4416809082031
      ],
      "text": "sensitive than the value of > 10 mg/L. The meta-analysis of data on individual patients on CRP with",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        401.19866943359375,
        527.3873291015625,
        415.6416931152344
      ],
      "text": "a cut-off of > 5 mg/L reported similar sensitivity and higher or similar specificity to the W4SS in all",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        206.48899841308594,
        414.39862060546875,
        238.00730895996094,
        428.8416442871094
      ],
      "text": "Table 3",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        414.39862060546875,
        527.3876953125,
        428.8417053222656
      ],
      "text": "). When CRP was combined with the W4SS and used in parallel,  the subpopulations assessed (",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86607360839844,
        427.5986328125,
        527.4041137695312,
        442.0416564941406
      ],
      "text": "it had similar or greater sensitivity and specificity than the W4SS alone in all populations, depending",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        440.7986145019531,
        527.5265502929688,
        455.24163818359375
      ],
      "text": "on the cut-off threshold used and the subpopulation assessed, while a positive screen with either tool",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.990546226501465,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        453.99859619140625,
        527.4091186523438,
        468.4416198730469
      ],
      "text": "led to a diagnostic test. CRP was found to be most accurate for outpatients who were not on ART as",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        467.1986083984375,
        527.4232788085938,
        481.6416320800781
      ],
      "text": "compared with the W4SS alone, which had a sensitivity of 84% (95% CI 75% ; 90%) and a specificity",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        480.39862060546875,
        527.1923217773438,
        494.8416442871094
      ],
      "text": "of 37% (95% CI 25% ; 50%) in this subpopulation. When performed sequentially after a positive W4SS",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.981284141540527,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        493.5986022949219,
        527.4443969726562,
        508.0416259765625
      ],
      "text": "in people with HIV who were not on ART, CRP with a cut-off of > 5 mg/L was as sensitive (84%; 95%",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        506.798583984375,
        527.437255859375,
        521.2415771484375
      ],
      "text": "CI 73% ; 90%) as the W4SS alone but was significantly more specific (64%; 95% CI 55 ; 72%). Like the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        519.9986572265625,
        527.4111328125,
        534.441650390625
      ],
      "text": "W4SS, the specificity of CRP for TB screening in inpatients with HIV was extremely low, probably due",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        533.1986083984375,
        465.8311462402344,
        547.6416015625
      ],
      "text": "to competing comorbidities that would also result in raised CRP levels and symptoms.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        554.7926025390625,
        527.4332275390625,
        569.3455810546875
      ],
      "text": "Recommendation 13  relates to use of mWRD for screening adults and adolescents with HIV for TB",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        568.1026000976562,
        527.3936157226562,
        582.5455932617188
      ],
      "text": "disease. A systematic review of the performance of mWRD in screening for TB among people with",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        581.302490234375,
        527.4453735351562,
        595.7454833984375
      ],
      "text": "HIV comprised 14 studies with a total of 9209 participants. The Xpert MTB/RIF assay was the mWRD",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        594.5025634765625,
        527.3748779296875,
        608.945556640625
      ],
      "text": "used in most of the studies. Use of an mWRD alone had a sensitivity of 69% (95% CI 60% ; 76%) and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        607.7025756835938,
        527.4400634765625,
        622.1455688476562
      ],
      "text": "a specificity of 98% (95% CI 97% ; 99%) as compared with use of the W4SS followed by an mWRD,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        620.902587890625,
        487.8069763183594,
        635.3455810546875
      ],
      "text": "which had sensitivity of 62% (95% CI 56% ; 69%) and a specificity of 99% (95% CI 97% ; 99%) (",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.97983169555664,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        487.77899169921875,
        620.902587890625,
        518.9454345703125,
        635.3455810546875
      ],
      "text": "Table 3",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.97983169555664,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        518.9146118164062,
        620.902587890625,
        527.4103393554688,
        635.3455810546875
      ],
      "text": ").",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.97983169555664,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        634.1025390625,
        527.3953857421875,
        648.5455322265625
      ],
      "text": "The accuracy of the mWRD was not significantly different from that of the W4SS followed by the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        647.302490234375,
        228.76016235351562,
        661.7454833984375
      ],
      "text": "mWRD in various subpopulations.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        454.0071105957031,
        801.0170288085938,
        554.0402221679688,
        811.52099609375
      ],
      "text": "1. Recommendations 13",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "heading"
    }
  ]
}